  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Ebelin lactone and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as the compound is linked through multiple pathways to this complex. Ebelin lactone acts as a target for several entities, including Leukocyte antigen CD37, which in turn is targeted by other compounds such as violaceol II and methyl 1-propenyl thiosulfinate. These latter compounds are also linked to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a possible cascade of interactions. The presence of multiple pathways with similar scores (final_score=0.558) suggests that Ebelin lactone may interact with the complex through various molecular mechanisms, possibly involving the modulation of epigenetic processes. The evidence is consistent across different molecular entities, highlighting a potential role for Ebelin lactone in influencing the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
